questions.question_text:
For the polynomial graph shown, determine the sign of the leading coefficient and whether the degree is odd or even.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3,0)--(3,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3)--(0,3) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-1.6:1.6,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{1-0.5*\x*\x*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shown is a cubic with leading coefficient $1$. Which equation represents it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-3.4,0)--(3.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3,0)--(0,3,0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-2.5:2.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=70] plot ({\x},{0.5*\x*(\x-2)*(\x+2)});
\fill (-2,0) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$-2$};
\fill (0,0) circle (2pt) node[above left] {$0$};
\fill (2,0) circle (2pt) node[below right] {$2$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

The graph shown is a cubic. Which equation represents it?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-4.4,0)--(5.4,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[<->] (0,-3.5)--(0,3.5) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick,blue,<->,domain=-3.62:4.51,smooth,variable=\x,samples=70] plot ({\x},{-0.1*(\x+3)*(\x-1)*(\x-4)});
\fill (-3,0) circle (2pt) node[below left] {$-3$};
\fill (1,0) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$1$};
\fill (4,0) circle (2pt) node[above right] {$4$};
\fill (0,-1.2) circle (2pt);
\node[anchor=east] at (-0.4,-3) {$(0,-24)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
